  "_comment": [
    "Named FiveM/GTA5 cheat families. This is what lets the scan say WHICH cheat",
    "was found instead of just 'something suspicious'.",
    "",
    "HOW MATCHING WORKS - read this before adding entries:",
    "  filename_contains / folder_contains: substring match. ONLY put distinctive",
    "    brand tokens here ('eulen', 'redengine'). Never a common word - putting",
    "    'stand' here would flag every file named 'standard_config.dll'.",
    "  filename_exact / process_exact / folder_exact: full name match, case",
    "    insensitive. Use this for short or common brand names.",
    "  sha256: exact file hashes. EMPTY BY DEFAULT ON PURPOSE - shipping made-up",
    "    hashes would create a scanner that looks thorough and detects nothing.",
    "    Add real ones as you collect samples; a hash match is the only indicator",
    "    that is treated as certain proof.",
    "",
    "LIMITS: these match the cheat's own naming. A cheat renamed to 'svchost.exe'",
    "or injected without touching disk will NOT match here - that is what the",
    "behavioural checks (injected memory, ghost modules, drivers) are for."
